Create IAM service accounts in Monitoring EKS

monitoring-eks
     │
     ├── thanos-s3
     │
     ├── loki-s3
     │
     └── tempo-s3


Make sure you are in monitoring eks cluster
kubectl config use-context monitoring-eks
kubectl config current-context


Create Thanos IAM service account:
=================================

eksctl create iamserviceaccount \
  --cluster monitoring-eks \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --namespace monitoring \
  --name thanos-s3 \
  --role-name ThanosS3Role \
  --attach-policy-arn arn:aws:iam::${AWS_ACCOUNT_ID}:policy/ThanosS3AccessPolicy \
  --approve


The above command automatically create monitoring namespace in monitoring cluster:

Create Loki IAM service account:
================================
eksctl create iamserviceaccount \
  --cluster monitoring-eks \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --namespace monitoring \
  --name loki-s3 \
  --role-name LokiS3Role \
  --attach-policy-arn arn:aws:iam::${AWS_ACCOUNT_ID}:policy/LokiS3AccessPolicy \
  --approve


